# Rockface Village. "{T}: Add {R}. Spend this mana only to cast a creature spell" (CR 106.6): on turn 1 that {R}, the only
# mana there is, can't cast Lightning Bolt (the refusal) but casts Blazing Rootwalla, a Lizard creature spell. Turn 3: Black
# Lotus's {R}{R}{R} casts a second Rootwalla, and "{R}, {T}: Target Lizard, Mouse, Otter, or Raccoon you control gets +1/+0
# and gains haste until end of turn" gives it haste the turn it arrived: it attacks as a 2/1 (Bot2 to 18). It can't target
# Ornithopter (a creature of Bot1's that is none of the four types) nor Bot2's own Rootwalla (a Lizard Bot1 doesn't control).
# "Activate only as a sorcery" (CR 602.5d): in Bot1's turn-5 upkeep, the Mountain and the Village untapped, it is not
# offered; in the main phase it is, on the first Rootwalla. Turn 7 "{T}: Add {C}" adds plain {C}, and the +1/+0 of turn 5
# is gone (until end of turn, CR 514.2).

